        "v": 5,
        "title": "Add TERMINALCOMMANDCOMPLETEDSINGLE analytics",
        "summary": "Added `TERMINAL_COMMAND_COMPLETED_SINGLE` enum value to `AnalyticsEvent` and triggered `trackEvent` within `runSinglePtyCommand` in `npm-app/src/terminal/base.ts`. This separates single PTY command completions from the existing `TERMINAL_COMMAND_COMPLETED` event, providing more granular telemetry for terminal usage. The change also reorders imports in `base.ts` for clarity.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-15T12:59:46.953Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "You won't see this directly, but the app now silently logs a second, more specific analytics event whenever it runs a single terminal command (like a one-off build or test run), separate from its existing tracking for completed terminal commands. The app will send this new event to analytics whenever a single PTY command finishes, tagging it with the command name and whether it was set to persist; behind the scenes, the tracking code in the terminal module was also reorganized by moving an import statement.",
